# Omarchy profile: one `omarchy` command per line (the leading "omarchy" is optional).
# Apply with `dot omarchy`: lines already in effect are skipped, the rest are
# shown in a picker. Quote arguments that contain spaces. See `omarchy commands`.
#
# dot can tell whether these are already done: default …, theme set, font set,
# webapp remove, tui remove, pkg add / aur add / drop. Anything else (e.g.
# `install …`) is listed as "can't check" and only runs when you tick it.

# ---- default apps (installs the app first if it's missing)
default browser chromium
default terminal ghostty
default editor zed
default agent claude

# ---- look
theme set "Tokyo Night"
font set "JetBrainsMono Nerd Font"

# ---- extra software through omarchy's installers
# install browser firefox
# install dev-env node
# install dev-env go
# install service tailscale
# install service 1password
# pkg add btop
# pkg aur add some-aur-package

# ---- preinstalls to remove (uncomment what you don't want)
# webapp remove Basecamp
# webapp remove HEY
# webapp remove WhatsApp
# webapp remove X
# webapp remove YouTube
# webapp remove Zoom
# webapp remove Discord
# webapp remove "Google Contacts"
# webapp remove "Google Maps"
# webapp remove "Google Messages"
# webapp remove "Google Photos"
# tui remove Docker
# pkg drop libreoffice-fresh
# pkg drop obsidian
# pkg drop pinta
# pkg drop moonlight-qt
# pkg drop aether cliamp omacut monologue omacalc omawrite hype signed
# remove preinstalls        # omarchy's own "remove all of the above" (asks first)
